{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "U3 and U4 module ports target the modern Spring stack (Java 17, Spring Boot 3.x, Spring Cloud Stream 4.x) following spring-cloud-stream-modules conventions: separate autoconfigure, starter, and app modules built with Maven.",
    "U2, U5, U6, U7 and U8 are implemented inside the existing Spring XD codebase (XD admin server REST layer and the AngularJS admin UI) without migrating XD to a new platform.",
    "U1 is implemented in Spring Cloud Stream core: the BinderFactory is extended to create multiple binder instances of the same binding type from per-binder configuration (spring.cloud.stream.binders.<binderName>.environment), bindings reference a binder by name (spring.cloud.stream.bindings.<bindingName>.binder), and single-binder configurations keep current default behavior for backward compatibility.",
    "U2 replaces NameNodeProxies.createNonHAProxy with a Hadoop FileSystem built from an HA-aware Configuration (dfs.nameservices, dfs.ha.namenodes.<ns>, dfs.namenode.rpc-address.*, dfs.client.failover.proxy.provider); the custom module registry resolves module archives through this HA-aware FileSystem, reusing spring-data-hadoop configuration support.",
    "U3 Cassandra sink uses Spring Data Cassandra / DataStax driver with upsert write semantics and configurable TTL and consistency level; integration tests run against embedded Cassandra / Testcontainers.",
    "U4 analytic-pmml processor uses the JPMML evaluator; the PMML model location is a configurable resource (file, classpath, or HDFS via the HA-aware FileSystem from U2); incoming JSON payloads are mapped to model input fields; tests use sample PMML models.",
    "U5 exposes GET /jobs/definitions/{name}/composition returning {name, composed: boolean}; U6 exposes GET /jobs/definitions/{name}/composition/graph returning a DTO with nodes (job names) and directed edges (parent-child) built by traversing the existing composed-job domain model; both are additive, backward-compatible HAL endpoints in the XD admin REST layer.",
    "U7/U8: the XD Admin UI jobs list consumes the composition flag endpoint to render an icon/badge with distinct styling for composed jobs, and row click routes to the composed-job detail/graph page or the single-job detail page accordingly; e2e coverage via Protractor.",
    "Testing strategy: JUnit/Mockito unit tests, Spring integration tests, Testcontainers/embedded resources for external systems, MiniDFSCluster in HA mode for HDFS; documentation in Asciidoc; no security/authentication changes."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single developer performs all work; estimates are effort in work-hours, not elapsed calendar duration; no parallelization or external code review is assumed.",
    "All relevant repositories (spring-xd, spring-xd-ambari, spring-cloud-stream and module repos) and a working build/CI environment are available, and the developer is experienced with the Spring ecosystem, Hadoop/HDFS and AngularJS.",
    "Scope is limited to the eight user stories (U1-U8); no unrelated refactoring or feature work is included.",
    "Done for each story means implementation plus unit/integration tests plus documentation merged; acceptance criteria are inferred from the story text.",
    "External systems are simulated in tests (embedded Cassandra/Testcontainers, sample PMML models, MiniDFSCluster with HA); no access to production clusters is required.",
    "REST API changes are additive and backward compatible; no authentication or authorization changes are needed.",
    "UI work is limited to the existing XD Admin UI jobs section; only lightweight mockups are needed, no formal UX design process.",
    "Artifact publishing to public repositories, production deployment, and performance/load testing are out of scope.",
    "Estimates include normal debugging and defect fixing; major defects in upstream third-party frameworks would be out of scope."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A-01",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and solution design",
      "activity_description": "Analyze the eight user stories, inspect existing spring-xd / spring-cloud-stream codebases, design the multi-binder configuration model, HDFS HA approach, module port structure, REST contracts and UI changes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-02",
      "activity_name": "Development environment and build/branch setup",
      "activity_description": "Set up local development environment, clones, feature branches and verify Maven builds for all affected repositories.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-03",
      "activity_name": "U1: Multi-binder configuration model and BinderFactory changes",
      "activity_description": "Implement per-binder configuration parsing (spring.cloud.stream.binders.*) and extend BinderFactory/BinderFactoryConfiguration to instantiate and cache multiple binder instances of the same type.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-04",
      "activity_name": "U1: BindingService integration and default binder fallback",
      "activity_description": "Wire named binders into BindingService so bindings can target a specific binder, with backward-compatible fallback to the single/default binder when none is specified.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-05",
      "activity_name": "U1: Unit and integration tests for multi-binder support",
      "activity_description": "Write unit and integration tests covering multiple binders of the same type, binder selection per binding, misconfiguration handling and default behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-06",
      "activity_name": "U1: Documentation and sample for multi-binder support",
      "activity_description": "Document the multi-binder configuration properties and add a sample showing reading from one system and writing to another using two binders of the same type.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-07",
      "activity_name": "U2: HA-aware HDFS configuration and custom module registry changes",
      "activity_description": "Replace non-HA proxy creation with an HA-aware Hadoop FileSystem (nameservices, HA namenodes, failover proxy provider) and update the XD custom module registry/loading to resolve modules from HDFS through it.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-08",
      "activity_name": "U2: HDFS HA integration tests",
      "activity_description": "Add integration tests using MiniDFSCluster in HA mode verifying custom module location resolution and failover behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-09",
      "activity_name": "U2: HDFS HA documentation",
      "activity_description": "Document the HDFS HA configuration properties for custom module locations in XD/Ambari docs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-10",
      "activity_name": "U3: Port and adapt Cassandra module to s-c-s sink",
      "activity_description": "Port the XD cassandra module code to a Spring Cloud Stream sink application using @EnableBinding(Sink.class), adapting options and lifecycle.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-11",
      "activity_name": "U3: Cassandra sink configuration properties and starter packaging",
      "activity_description": "Create configuration properties class, autoconfigure module, starter and app packaging in the s-c-s modules repository structure.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-12",
      "activity_name": "U3: Cassandra sink integration tests",
      "activity_description": "Implement integration tests against embedded Cassandra/Testcontainers covering writes, TTL/consistency options and error cases.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-13",
      "activity_name": "U3: Cassandra sink documentation",
      "activity_description": "Write reference documentation/README for the Cassandra sink including options and usage in a streaming pipeline.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-14",
      "activity_name": "U4: Port and adapt analytic-pmml module to s-c-s processor",
      "activity_description": "Port the XD analytic-pmml module to a Spring Cloud Stream processor using @EnableBinding(Processor.class) with JPMML-based evaluation and configurable model location.",
      "most_likely_effort": 14
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-15",
      "activity_name": "U4: PMML processor packaging and dependency setup",
      "activity_description": "Set up autoconfigure/starter/app modules, JPMML dependencies and resource resolution (file/classpath/HDFS HA) for the model.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-16",
      "activity_name": "U4: PMML processor tests",
      "activity_description": "Write unit and integration tests with sample PMML models covering input mapping, evaluation output and error handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-17",
      "activity_name": "U4: PMML processor documentation",
      "activity_description": "Document the analytic-pmml processor options and pipeline usage.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-18",
      "activity_name": "U5: Job composition flag service logic",
      "activity_description": "Implement service-layer logic in XD admin determining whether a job definition is standalone or part of a composed job.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-19",
      "activity_name": "U5: Composition flag REST controller, DTO and tests",
      "activity_description": "Add GET endpoint returning the composition flag, define the response DTO, and add MVC/integration tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-20",
      "activity_name": "U6: Composition graph model and traversal logic",
      "activity_description": "Design the graph DTO (nodes and directed parent-child edges) and implement traversal of the composed-job domain model to build the graph.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-21",
      "activity_name": "U6: Composition graph REST controller, DTO and tests",
      "activity_description": "Expose the graph via a GET endpoint in the XD admin REST layer and add MVC/integration tests including nested compositions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 14
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-22",
      "activity_name": "U7: Admin UI job list differentiation",
      "activity_description": "Update the AngularJS XD Admin UI jobs list to consume the composition flag endpoint and visually distinguish composed jobs from single jobs with an icon/badge and styling; add e2e test coverage.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-23",
      "activity_name": "U8: Admin UI detail-page navigation for composed and single jobs",
      "activity_description": "Implement click-through routing so selecting a job navigates to the composed-job detail/graph view or the single-job detail page as appropriate; add e2e tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-24",
      "activity_name": "End-to-end integration, system testing and defect fixing",
      "activity_description": "Integrate all changes across repositories, run full builds and end-to-end scenarios (multi-binder pipeline, HDFS HA module loading, composed-job REST and UI flows), and fix defects.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-25",
      "activity_name": "Final documentation updates and release preparation",
      "activity_description": "Consolidate reference documentation, update changelogs and prepare the increment for merge/release.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 296
  }
}

